<h3>EBMC Stop</h3>
<form class="form-horizontal" onsubmit="return false;">
    <div class="control-group">
        <div class="controls">
            <label class="checkbox">
                <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.plugins.ebmc_stop.heaters_off">
                Switch heaters off first (M104 S0, M140 S0)
            </label>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="control-group">
        <label class="control-label">After-stop G-code</label>
        <div class="controls">
            <textarea rows="6" class="input-block-level" style="font-family: monospace"
                      data-bind="value: settings.plugins.ebmc_stop.after_stop_gcode"></textarea>
            <span class="help-block">
                Sent only once the print has been cancelled and the printer is idle
                (after OctoPrint's own "after print job is cancelled" script).
                One command per line. Lines starting with ";" are ignored. Each line is
                upper-cased (except the text of M117/M118 messages). Lines that do not start with G, M or T followed by a
                number (for example G28, M104, T0) are skipped and logged, because
                Smoothieware would run them as console commands.
            </span>
            <span class="help-block">
                <strong>Why the default is only G28:</strong> on this printer Z homes
                <em>upwards</em> (to Z max) first, so G28 already lifts the nozzle away
                from the part before X and Y move, and a relative lift near the top of
                travel would drive into the stop. On a printer that homes Z
                <em>downwards</em> onto the bed, plain G28 can crash the nozzle into the
                part: do not use this default there.
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
</form>
